n> until <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w32">eventually</span> it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w34">produces</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w33">consequence</span>. Thus, they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w40">say</span>, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w37">consequence</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w35">original</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w36">karma</span> is something that is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w39">produced</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w38">indirectly</span>, via a medium. This <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w41">same</span> type of idea applies to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w42">other</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w43">three</span> positions expressed.<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s224w11"><span class="nul">Cessation predicate has no separately alignable exponent in this English row; the timing phrase does not mean ceased.</span></span></span>
